# Copy to .env and adjust as needed.

# ---- Active data root for the pipeline steps ----
# Where the canonical 12-class audio and pipeline artifacts live: the step scripts read and write
# here. Defaults to <repo>/all-samples (Philharmonia) if unset. Point it at the shared cluster
# dataset root, an external drive, or the TinySOL root below.
# RISE_DATA_ROOT=/path/to/data-root

# ---- Per-dataset roots ----
# Each mirrors the same layout (pipeline/ tracked in git; work/, features/, checkpoints/ ignored).
# Philharmonia, 12-class, fetched by `python -m instrument_robustness.prep_data`.
# RISE_PHIL_ROOT=/path/to/all-samples
# TinySOL, the same 12 classes but lossless WAV isolated notes, indexed by
# `python -m instrument_robustness.build_tinysol_manifest`.
# RISE_TINYSOL_ROOT=/path/to/tinysol

# To run the pipeline on TinySOL instead of Philharmonia, only the root changes -- both datasets
# use the same canonical 12 labels, so no label override is needed:
#   RISE_DATA_ROOT="$RISE_TINYSOL_ROOT" python -m instrument_robustness.step0_filter

# ---- Class set (comma-separated) ----
# Defaults to config.CANONICAL_LABELS (the alphabetical 12). Overriding this changes label indices
# and invalidates saved checkpoints, so only set it deliberately.
# RISE_TARGET_LABELS=bassoon,cello,clarinet,double-bass,flute,french-horn,oboe,trombone,trumpet,tuba,viola,violin

# ---- Noise sweep ----
# Where the ESC-50 real-noise clips live (kept out of git). Used by noise_sweep.py.
# RISE_NOISE_ROOT=/path/to/noise_sources
